{% comment %}
  The two maps are made by scripts/build_coffee_map.py from the Google My Maps export; after changing
  the map, export a new KMZ and run the script again. Both SVGs are inlined, so they make no requests,
  and hidden from screen readers: the intro, the legend and the full-map link say what they show.
{% endcomment %}
<section class="elsewhere-section coffee-atlas" id="coffee-atlas">
  <h2>Coffee Atlas</h2>
  <p class="section-intro">Cafés I’ve loved&nbsp;❤️ and ones that do the job for a daily coffee&nbsp;⭐.</p>

  <div class="coffee-atlas-maps">
    <div class="coffee-atlas-map coffee-atlas-japan">{% include coffee-atlas-japan.svg %}</div>
    <div class="coffee-atlas-map coffee-atlas-usa">{% include coffee-atlas-usa.svg %}</div>
  </div>

  <div class="coffee-atlas-footer">
    <ul class="coffee-atlas-legend">
      <li><span class="coffee-atlas-key coffee-atlas-key-loved" aria-hidden="true"></span>Loved&nbsp;❤️</li>
      <li><span class="coffee-atlas-key coffee-atlas-key-daily" aria-hidden="true"></span>Daily coffee&nbsp;⭐</li>
    </ul>
    <a class="action-link external-link" href="https://www.google.com/maps/d/viewer?mid=1H58JGmucJ3DXcAVr82gdeM_ekxaunUE">Open the full map&nbsp;↗</a>
  </div>
</section>
